usage: render.py [-h] -o OUTPUT [--preview] [--draft] [--build-subtitles]
                 [--no-subtitles] [--no-loudnorm] [--fps FPS]
                 edl

Render a video from an EDL

positional arguments:
  edl                   Path to edl.json

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -o OUTPUT, --output OUTPUT
                        Output video path
  --preview             Preview mode: 1080p, medium, CRF 22 — evaluable for
                        QC, faster than final.
  --draft               Draft mode: 720p, ultrafast, CRF 28 — cut-point
                        verification only.
  --build-subtitles     Build master.srt from transcripts + EDL offsets before
                        compositing
  --no-subtitles        Skip subtitles even if the EDL references one
  --no-loudnorm         Skip audio loudness normalization. Default is on (-14
                        LUFS, -1 dBTP, LRA 11).
  --fps FPS             Output frame rate. Default: preserve the source's
                        frame rate (falls back to 24 if it can't be probed).
                        Pass e.g. --fps 30 or --fps 30000/1001 to force.
